{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And we passed by our brethren, etc.</b> The reason Scripture mentions them with brotherhood is to say that they fulfilled the word of HaShem who commanded them not to wage war against them, and they journeyed away from them in brotherhood. Further, Scripture calls them <b>our brethren</b> because they acted toward Israel with brotherhood, selling them bread and water and food, as it is written (Deuteronomy 2:29): ״כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשׂוּ לִי בְּנֵי עֵשָׂו״ and so forth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:28.769814591Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}